      "side": 1,
      "message": "I can see how this can work for the flags that should be eliminated with no replacement when using an OpenJDK 8 toolchain.\n\nHowever:\n\n1. it\u0027s not documented, but currently the makefiles distinguish between:\nEXPERIMENTAL_USE_OPENJDK9\u003dtrue means to build with OpenJDK 9 and target language version 1.9 (this means that -bootclasspath is no longer supported but --system is).\n\nEXPERIMENTAL_USE_OPENJDK9\u003dtarget1.8 (or any other value) means to build with OpenJDK 9 and target language version 1.8 (this means that -bootclasspath is still supported).\n\n2. Having this in here might make it less obvious why makefiles that add these OpenJDK 9 specific flags work when building with OpenJDK 8.\n\n3.) This doesn\u0027t work for other kinds of flags where specific different versions exist for 8 vs. 9 (e.g. -bootclasspath vs. --system).\n\nAt present I\u0027m not convinced that this CL adds enough convenience value to be worth the cost of these limitations. I could be convinced if some additional use cases exist to tip the balance.",
